shown excellent results. Maglab in the USA obtained 32 T in 2018, which is the only magnet over 30 T, and used it in the insulation process [1]. For the no-insulation process, the RIKEN and SuNAM achieved 30.5 and 26.4 T, respectively [2, 3]. In 2019, the Institute of Electrical Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences (IEE, CAS) obtained 32.35 T, which is the world record of magnetic field strength for a single superconductor magnet [4].
As the normal zone progress velocity of REBCO is at the level of millimeters per second, the quench protection system in the insulation process is more complicated than that of the common NbTi coil. In the no-insulation process, the current can be bypassed in the radial direction, which provides the REBCO coils with a self-protection ability. However, the

