We established the first database of the effect of Cu stabilizers on different commercial REBCO tapes on both resistivity and thermal conductivity. The charging loss and self-protection ability were also evaluated. However, three points required attention. Substantial amounts of data have been shown above, but without either the resistivity or the thermal conductivity with the parameters of the Cu stabilizer. Therefore, we evaluated whether the difference in resistivity or thermal conductivity truthfully reflects the effect of the Cu stabilizer, or whether there are measurement errors that interrupt the resistivity or the thermal conductivity. Thus, we first calculated the measurement accuracy. The relationship between the resistivity or thermal conductivity and the Cu stabilizer could not be ascertained even after incorporating the measurement error. Second, we looked beyond the thickness, surface roughness, and purity of the Cu stabilizer, which can significantly affect the resistivity or thermal conductivity of different commercial tapes. We then identified the applications of our database.
4.1. Measurement error
All of our data were measured using the same equipment by the same person. Therefore, the equipment measurement error may have only affected the absolute value of all the samples instead of the difference between different samples. Here, the measurement error that we want to discuss is the error from sample preparation. As all the samples were also prepared by the same process and same person, it is possible that the sample condition could have affected the preparation and interrupted the measurement data. The resistivity and thermal conductivity in the circumferential direction of SZ1, SZ2, and SZ3 are good examples of the same. From tables 1 and 2, it can be observed that the surface roughness was the only difference among these three samples, and were 1193.00 ± 20.46, 170.67 ± 6.55, and 50.65 ± 8.50, respectively. Indeed, SZ1 and SZ2 had higher surface roughness than SZ3. According to the information from the company, one method is physical,

